This question is weird.
It asks for almost missing integer `x`

Where almost missing means, that `x` appears in exactly one window of length k

so if x appears in two different windows like 
`[9,2,x]` and `[2,1,x]` then x is not "almost missing"

if `x` comes in [9,x,x] and no where else, `x` is almost missing.

and we have to return  largest almost missing integer from nums.
and -1, if none exist.


So we know, only first and last element couldn't be repeated, any integers in windows from middle, will always be repeated.

`[3,9,2,1,7`] -> [3,9,2] [9,2,1] [2,1,7]` for k = 3

so we can take firstCount, which counts starting integer if it exist in a window ie nums[0]
and same for `lastCount`  ie nums[nums.length-1]

so from 0....nums.length-k
we check in each window (i, i+k)
`if(window.includes(nums[0])) firstCount++`
`if(window.includes(nums[nums.length - 1])) lastCount++`

initialise ans = -1
so if firstCount is 1, we take max of ans, nums[0]

and if lastCount is 1, we do the same `Math.max(ans, nums[nums.length - 1]);`

return ans.


EDGE CASES:
1) if k === nums.length, then whole nums is a window
so we directly return max num from it. 
since, all integers are coming in that window, largest will be the `return Math.max(...nums)`

2) if k === 1 

that means, every window is of size 1, ie is basically the integers in nums array itself.

so, we make hashMap, and take frequency.

now, we loop of hasMap, for `[val, frequency]`
and we dont consider, whose frequency > 1

and consider others, and take `max = Math.max(max, val)`

since we dont want the repeating ones, since every window is of size 1.

```js
/**
 * @param {number[]} nums
 * @param {number} k
 * @return {number}
 */
var largestInteger = function(nums, k) {
    if(k === nums.length) return Math.max(...nums)

    if(k === 1){
        let map = new Map()

        nums.forEach((item) => map.set(item, (map.get(item) ?? 0 ) + 1))

        let max = -1
        for(let [val, fr] of map){
            if(fr === 1){
                max = Math.max(max, val)
            }
        }

        return max
    }

    let firstCount = 0
    let lastCount = 0

    for(let i = 0; i<=nums.length - k; i++){

        let window = nums.slice(i, i+k)

        if(window.includes(nums[0])) firstCount++

        if(window.includes(nums[nums.length - 1])) lastCount++
    }

    let ans = -1;

    if (firstCount === 1) {
        ans = Math.max(ans, nums[0]);
    }

    if (lastCount === 1) {
        ans = Math.max(ans, nums[nums.length - 1]);
    }

    return ans;

};
```

